WEBVTT

00:00.790 --> 00:01.720
Maple!

00:01.720 --> 00:02.970
This was your doing, wasn't it?

00:03.790 --> 00:05.380
You can't play dumb with me!

00:05.690 --> 00:09.830
How could you do this to me 
while I was asleep?!

00:11.590 --> 00:13.070
Where's your sorry?

00:13.970 --> 00:16.370
<i>I'm... sorry.</i>

00:17.210 --> 00:20.500
<i>But Master busy.</i>

00:21.060 --> 00:22.750
<i>Lonely.</i>

00:23.590 --> 00:24.790
I see.

00:25.630 --> 00:30.640
I have been focused on potion making
and other work, lately...

00:32.260 --> 00:34.070
I'm sorry, too.

00:34.490 --> 00:37.810
I'll take a break from work 
today and play with you!

00:38.220 --> 00:39.800
<i>Play!</i>

00:39.800 --> 00:43.880
<i>Play! Play! Play!</i>

00:40.590 --> 00:42.880
Takumi!

00:43.690 --> 00:45.540
I've brought you lunch.

00:49.680 --> 00:51.420
Whoa! It's not what you think!

00:51.420 --> 00:55.200
It's not like Maple was trying 
to eat me as prey or anything!

00:56.960 --> 00:58.120
This...

00:58.120 --> 01:00.570
is spider silk, isn't it?!

02:34.170 --> 02:39.260
<b>Episode 2
To a New Land</b>

02:34.170 --> 02:39.260
<b>Episode 2
To a New Land</b>

02:34.230 --> 02:36.880
This is wonderful!

02:37.130 --> 02:40.130
I can't believe we got to make 
clothes from spider silk!

02:40.130 --> 02:42.190
Oh, the texture is perfect!

02:42.190 --> 02:44.200
Maple, you're the best!

02:44.620 --> 02:47.510
Is spider silk <i>that</i> amazing?

02:47.510 --> 02:48.380
Of course!

02:48.380 --> 02:49.850
It's a luxury item!

02:49.850 --> 02:52.470
The nobles always buy it all up!

02:52.470 --> 02:54.710
Maple, you're the best!

02:52.470 --> 02:55.190
Maple, you're incredible.

02:55.190 --> 02:56.500
Maple!

02:56.500 --> 02:59.640
Can you produce thread with 
a bit more elasticity?

02:59.640 --> 03:02.650
Oh, Maple can't understand speech.

03:02.650 --> 03:05.870
More e...las...ti...city!

03:06.240 --> 03:07.170
Understand?

03:07.170 --> 03:08.080
Can you make it?

03:10.910 --> 03:14.040
Great! This is it!

03:14.360 --> 03:17.510
They're actually... communicating?

03:18.040 --> 03:22.280
Maple, um, about playing with me?

03:23.140 --> 03:24.910
<i>Busy now.</i>

03:25.340 --> 03:27.050
Right...

03:28.630 --> 03:31.320
<i>Well, as long as Maple
is enjoying herself,</i>

03:31.320 --> 03:34.020
<i>I have my own things to 
do anyway, so it's fine.</i>

03:36.040 --> 03:38.840
<i>It's been nearly a month since 
I came to this village.</i>

03:38.840 --> 03:42.540
<i>I want to head to the city 
and study alchemy soon.</i>

03:42.540 --> 03:43.290
<i>But...</i>

03:43.290 --> 03:45.860
<i>What am I supposed to say to everyone?</i>

03:45.860 --> 03:47.360
<i>They've all been so kind to me.</i>

03:48.440 --> 03:49.560
Alright!

03:49.560 --> 03:51.110
How's the sizing?

03:52.180 --> 03:54.020
It's a perfect fit!

03:54.020 --> 03:59.290
I'll need to reinforce the 
soles and toes of the boots.

03:59.870 --> 04:02.190
You'll need it when you kick things, right?

04:02.190 --> 04:03.620
Kick things?

04:03.620 --> 04:06.090
But I'm a producer.

04:06.770 --> 04:11.280
There isn't a single producer who can 
wander into a forest full of monsters alone.

04:11.630 --> 04:13.770
Is that so?

04:13.770 --> 04:16.490
Oh, you finally finished the armor?

04:16.810 --> 04:17.720
Yeah.

04:17.720 --> 04:19.960
Just some minor adjustments left.

04:20.430 --> 04:22.280
It'll be lonely without you.

04:22.280 --> 04:22.940
Huh?

04:23.300 --> 04:24.500
You're moving on, right?

04:24.500 --> 04:25.900
Going to the next place.

04:26.300 --> 04:29.450
In order for your production job to grow,

04:29.450 --> 04:31.880
you should to to a city 
where demand will be higher

04:31.880 --> 04:34.230
and there will be a more
 reliable supply of materials.

04:34.880 --> 04:35.770
Yes.

04:36.430 --> 04:40.170
It just so happens that a trader from 
Bolton is coming here next week.

04:40.660 --> 04:41.920
From Bolton?

04:42.340 --> 04:47.040
We've already arranged for 
you to ride on his carriage.

04:48.330 --> 04:49.550
Banga...

04:50.020 --> 04:50.910
Alright!

04:50.910 --> 04:54.990
Now that that's settled, 
let's get this finished up quick!

04:54.990 --> 04:56.170
Bobon...

04:56.820 --> 04:58.080
Both of you...

04:59.160 --> 05:00.890
Thank you so much!

05:04.410 --> 05:06.000
Martha!

05:06.890 --> 05:08.320
Takumi.

05:08.320 --> 05:09.330
What's that?

05:09.330 --> 05:12.780
The innards of a Horned 
Rabbit Banga hunted.

05:13.110 --> 05:15.520
Apparently they're the most delicious part,

05:15.520 --> 05:19.400
but they need to be processed properly 
to remove any diseases and parasites.

05:19.400 --> 05:23.020
We're not able to do that here,
 so we have to throw them away.

05:23.020 --> 05:25.710
I can use purification magic, though.

05:26.100 --> 05:26.950
Huh?

05:28.660 --> 05:30.080
<i>Purification.</i>

05:32.110 --> 05:34.340
It should be edible now.

05:35.270 --> 05:40.120
Takumi, you can use light magic?

05:40.690 --> 05:41.550
Yes.

05:41.890 --> 05:43.110
Thank you.

05:43.110 --> 05:45.620
Thanks to you, these won't 
have to go to waste.

05:45.620 --> 05:46.310
Though...

05:47.390 --> 05:51.450
It might be better not to show
 that magic to just anyone.

05:51.450 --> 05:53.300
Huh? Why not?

05:53.630 --> 05:58.120
Apparently, only a few people
can use light magic.

05:58.120 --> 05:59.610
It's rare enough

05:59.610 --> 06:02.390
that those with enough skill can 
make their living off that alone.

06:03.020 --> 06:04.880
I didn't know that.

06:05.470 --> 06:08.320
No one in this village will pay it any mind,

06:08.320 --> 06:11.240
but you should be careful once 
you're out of the village.

06:12.890 --> 06:15.550
<i>Earth magic, activate.</i>

06:18.610 --> 06:23.420
<i>I spent the next week pouring all of my 
power into Bord Village's development.</i>

06:24.360 --> 06:28.190
<i>I want to make it as safe as
 I can for the villagers to live in,</i>

06:29.100 --> 06:31.830
<i>and as convenient as possible, too.</i>

06:36.100 --> 06:40.860
<i>I want to repay them 
for all they've done for me.</i>

06:45.330 --> 06:47.510
Now this...

06:48.020 --> 06:49.970
Hey, Papek.

06:49.970 --> 06:52.930
Good afternoon, Mr. Banga.

06:54.270 --> 06:56.130
Is that everything you ordered?

06:56.130 --> 06:56.900
Yeah.

06:56.900 --> 06:58.220
Very well, then.

06:58.220 --> 07:00.390
We'll be waiting for your next order.

07:00.390 --> 07:01.430
Banga!

07:01.920 --> 07:03.850
All set, Takumi?

07:04.560 --> 07:06.920
Oh, this man is...

07:07.290 --> 07:09.570
Yeah. This is Takumi,
 the guy I told you about.

07:09.920 --> 07:11.040
It's a pleasure to meet you.

07:11.040 --> 07:13.620
I run a trading company in Bolton.

07:13.620 --> 07:15.730
My name is Papek.

07:15.730 --> 07:17.300
I'm Takumi Iruma.

07:17.300 --> 07:18.780
Thank you for taking me.

07:18.780 --> 07:20.720
Did you forget anything?

07:20.720 --> 07:22.000
I'm good.

07:22.400 --> 07:24.550
Oh, also, here.

07:25.940 --> 07:29.620
I had a hundred of the same 
delivered to your house.

07:29.620 --> 07:32.580
If anything happens, please 
distribute them amongst everyone.

07:34.470 --> 07:35.510
This is a big help.

07:35.510 --> 07:36.800
Thank you.

07:36.800 --> 07:39.690
Is that... a potion?

07:40.130 --> 07:42.680
Yes. They're basic healing potions.

07:43.030 --> 07:44.600
You made them?

07:44.600 --> 07:45.570
Yes.

07:45.570 --> 07:46.890
May I take a look?

07:54.120 --> 07:55.290
Takumi.

07:55.570 --> 07:56.700
It's finally time.

07:57.060 --> 07:58.210
Everyone...

07:58.740 --> 08:02.010
I'll be waiting in the carriage, then.

08:03.560 --> 08:04.950
Where's Maple?

08:05.290 --> 08:07.880
I'm sorry. She's asleep.

08:07.880 --> 08:09.670
Maple...

08:09.670 --> 08:10.830
Bye-bye.

08:11.550 --> 08:12.610
Takumi.

08:12.970 --> 08:14.410
Take care of yourself.

08:15.030 --> 08:16.510
Stay well.

08:17.550 --> 08:18.450
Yes.

08:19.320 --> 08:20.680
Takumi.

08:21.670 --> 08:22.610
Here.

08:25.330 --> 08:26.610
What's this?

08:26.970 --> 08:28.810
I'm glad! It fits perfectly!

08:28.810 --> 08:30.110
It looks good on you.

08:30.110 --> 08:32.460
Mister Takumi, you look so cool!

08:32.930 --> 08:36.900
We all made it together 
to thank you, Takumi.

08:36.900 --> 08:39.370
We had Maple produce the threads for it.

08:40.140 --> 08:42.870
I designed the pattern!

08:43.410 --> 08:44.910
Thank you.

08:44.910 --> 08:46.320
I'll treasure it!

08:47.130 --> 08:50.400
Everyone, our time together was short,

08:51.040 --> 08:53.910
but I truly appreciate 
all you've done for me!

09:00.880 --> 09:03.590
We'll leave your home just as it is, okay?

09:01.680 --> 09:06.220
Mister, don't forget about me!

09:03.610 --> 09:05.370
Come back anytime!

09:06.650 --> 09:07.780
Takumi!

09:07.260 --> 09:08.420
Everyone...

09:07.780 --> 09:09.320
Be careful!

09:09.330 --> 09:10.610
See you later!

09:10.610 --> 09:13.200
Farewell!

09:13.200 --> 09:14.540
<i>Thank you.</i>

09:14.540 --> 09:18.610
<i>This was the first place 
I lived in Mildgard.</i>

09:19.010 --> 09:20.280
<i>It's my hometown!</i>

09:25.700 --> 09:30.120
You sure are loved by the 
villagers, Mr. Takumi.

09:30.500 --> 09:35.280
You're practically family 
to those villagers.

09:35.590 --> 09:38.210
Whoa, are you crying, Heath?

09:38.210 --> 09:41.240
That kind of stuff gets to me.

09:41.240 --> 09:43.420
You sound like an old man.

09:44.590 --> 09:46.910
We haven't introduced ourselves yet, huh?

09:47.280 --> 09:48.380
I'm Heath.

09:48.800 --> 09:50.130
I'm Riell.

09:50.130 --> 09:52.440
Silent and gloomy over here is Bogar.

09:52.440 --> 09:53.620
Nice to meet you.

09:54.140 --> 09:59.410
They're the rank C adventuring 
party known as Lion Fang.

09:59.410 --> 10:02.320
Oh, you're bodyguards for Papek, then?

10:02.320 --> 10:03.210
Yeah.

10:03.210 --> 10:07.150
It's relatively peaceful around 
here, so it's a little boring.

10:07.150 --> 10:10.050
I wouldn't mind if a few 
monsters popped out.

10:10.050 --> 10:12.830
<i>No, I'd rather that </i>didn't<i> happen.</i>

10:13.930 --> 10:17.170
You're holding onto that bag 
like it's awfully precious.

10:17.170 --> 10:19.510
Oh, my pet Killer Spider's in it.

10:19.510 --> 10:20.970
A Killer Spider?!

10:20.970 --> 10:23.220
You <i>tamed</i> a spider?!

10:23.220 --> 10:25.440
Wow! Let us see!

10:25.780 --> 10:28.640
Hey there, Killer Spider.

10:29.670 --> 10:30.780
Ah!

10:31.340 --> 10:33.810
Maple! How could you?!

10:33.810 --> 10:36.020
No, Riell was in the wrong there.

10:36.020 --> 10:38.310
Assaulting her in her sleep is the worst.

10:38.310 --> 10:40.540
Phrasing! I wasn't assaulting her, either!

10:41.120 --> 10:43.750
What are you going to do if this causes her

10:43.750 --> 10:46.010
to start fearing humans 
or the outside world?

10:47.040 --> 10:49.250
She's really taken a liking to Bogar!

10:49.470 --> 10:50.990
That's a father for you.

10:50.990 --> 10:52.720
He has a different air about him.

10:52.720 --> 10:54.300
Mr. Takumi.

10:52.720 --> 10:55.800
Let me hug Maple, too!

10:54.300 --> 10:55.330
Yes?

10:55.330 --> 10:57.810
It's about the potions from earlier.

10:55.800 --> 10:58.030
<i>This guy, don't like!</i>

10:57.810 --> 10:59.590
Do you have any in stock?

11:00.100 --> 11:04.300
If you're willing, I'd like 
to buy them from you.

11:04.300 --> 11:07.010
I don't mind that.

11:07.390 --> 11:09.840
Maple, don't be too rude.

11:12.170 --> 11:13.680
Ow!

11:14.240 --> 11:16.740
Oh? Have some monsters shown up?

11:16.740 --> 11:18.330
This is how it ought to be.

11:18.330 --> 11:19.940
Makes the guard duty worth it.

11:20.230 --> 11:21.140
Huh?

11:27.770 --> 11:29.490
G-Goblins?!

11:29.860 --> 11:31.680
Takumi. Sit back.

11:35.250 --> 11:37.740
There's roughly twenty more in the forest.

11:37.740 --> 11:38.970
I'll smoke them out.

11:38.970 --> 11:40.030
Okay.

11:40.300 --> 11:42.480
I-I-It's alright.

11:42.480 --> 11:47.160
This is a r-regular o-occurrence 
for t-traveling m-m-merchants.

11:46.350 --> 11:47.810
<i>You seem really panicked despite that.</i>

11:47.810 --> 11:49.000
Here we go!

12:01.280 --> 12:03.550
Good. All done clearing them out.

12:03.550 --> 12:06.230
That took more time than I expected.

12:06.460 --> 12:10.960
Alright, let's dissect them quick 
and collect their magic stones.

12:10.960 --> 12:13.100
<i>Bogar, cool.</i>

12:13.100 --> 12:15.020
<i>Riell, don't like.</i>

12:15.020 --> 12:16.920
<i>Heath, neutral.</i>

12:18.490 --> 12:22.380
<i>Our peaceful journey continued 
without incident after that.</i>

12:22.840 --> 12:24.790
<i>Three days later...</i>

12:25.090 --> 12:29.810
<b>Bolton, Kingdom of Barcula</b>

12:25.320 --> 12:27.730
We're here, Mr. Takumi.

12:27.730 --> 12:29.800
Welcome to Bolton.

12:30.900 --> 12:35.370
<i>Everything looked so new in the 
first big city I visited.</i>

12:37.420 --> 12:41.580
<i>I headed for the Adventurer's Guild along 
with the three members of Lion Fang,</i>

12:41.580 --> 12:44.090
<i>who were going to report the 
success of their escort quest.</i>

12:45.870 --> 12:49.050
<i>I needed to register with the Guild 
in order to stay in the city,</i>

12:49.050 --> 12:51.640
<i>and to register Maple as a pet.</i>

12:53.540 --> 12:57.850
<i>I would have preferred to register with 
an alchemist's guild if possible...</i>

12:58.330 --> 13:02.200
Unfortunately, there isn't one here.

13:02.200 --> 13:03.250
Huh?!

13:03.790 --> 13:06.540
<i>Apparently, many people register 
with the Adventurer's Guild</i>

13:06.540 --> 13:10.050
<i>to use the guild card 
as their identification.</i>

13:10.050 --> 13:13.310
<i>Hans, the receptionist, 
whispered that into my ear.</i>

13:14.150 --> 13:16.080
<i>If I'm fine staying at the lowest rank,</i>

13:16.080 --> 13:19.890
<i>then apparently it won't expire as long 
as I accept a simple quest once a month.</i>

13:20.710 --> 13:24.030
<i>In the end, I decided to register 
with the Adventurer's Guild</i>

13:24.580 --> 13:26.760
<i>and register Maple as a pet.</i>

13:27.780 --> 13:30.240
<b>Papek Company</b>

13:30.250 --> 13:33.280
So I do have roughly a hundred of each in stock.

13:35.440 --> 13:37.540
That's wonderful.

13:37.540 --> 13:42.160
Then how about ten silver for each 
healing potion and stamina potion,

13:42.160 --> 13:46.390
and fifty silver for each mana potion?

13:46.390 --> 13:47.220
Huh?!

13:47.220 --> 13:49.640
<b>Understand at a Glance!\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hby Nolyn</b>

13:47.220 --> 13:49.640
<b>Understand at a Glance!\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hby Nolyn</b>

13:47.220 --> 13:49.640
<b>Mildgard's Currency Conversion</b>

13:47.220 --> 13:49.640
<b>Mildgard's Currency Conversion</b>

13:47.720 --> 13:49.640
<b>Silver</b>

13:47.720 --> 13:49.640
<b>Copper</b>

13:48.220 --> 13:49.640
<b>Silver</b>

13:48.220 --> 13:49.640
<b>Gold</b>

13:48.720 --> 13:49.640
<b>Gold</b>

13:48.720 --> 13:49.640
<b>Platinum</b>

13:51.000 --> 13:53.670
<i>That's like seven million yen 
in Japanese currency!</i>

13:53.670 --> 13:55.730
Hey, isn't that a lot?!

13:55.730 --> 13:59.430
Actually, I'm sorry to say 
I offered a slightly lower price

13:59.430 --> 14:02.170
since you haven't
made a name for yourself.

14:02.170 --> 14:04.040
R-Really?

14:04.650 --> 14:07.540
<i>This all sounds too good to be true.</i>

14:07.940 --> 14:11.150
<i>Why do this much
 for someone he just met?</i>

14:11.150 --> 14:12.870
<i>Does he have an ulterior motive?</i>

14:13.230 --> 14:16.410
<i>But he doesn't seem like the 
type to deceive others.</i>

14:16.410 --> 14:19.700
By the way, about your residence...

14:20.340 --> 14:22.160
My residence?

14:22.160 --> 14:25.920
If you plan to set yourself 
up as a producer,

14:25.920 --> 14:29.460
then I would recommend living 
in a home with a workshop.

14:29.460 --> 14:30.190
A home?!

14:30.190 --> 14:31.580
No, no, no!

14:31.580 --> 14:35.380
I just arrived in this city, and I don't 
have the savings to buy a home!

14:35.740 --> 14:37.470
If you're happy renting,

14:37.470 --> 14:41.600
then our company could 
recommend a place.

14:41.600 --> 14:43.560
P-Please hold on.

14:45.410 --> 14:46.870
Thomas!

14:46.870 --> 14:49.430
Take Mr. Takumi and show him
 the home we discussed.

14:50.530 --> 14:51.380
Wait.

14:51.380 --> 14:53.800
This is definitely a mansion!

14:53.800 --> 14:56.770
Yes. It's a highly recommended property.

14:57.160 --> 14:59.490
You recommend it, but—

14:59.490 --> 15:04.210
The rent is 1 gold and 50 silver a month.

15:05.170 --> 15:06.950
<i>That's certainly cheap.</i>

15:07.560 --> 15:10.920
Um, no one has died here, right?

15:10.920 --> 15:13.630
Not at all. We recommend it.

15:14.090 --> 15:16.800
<i>It looks like I could use that 
storehouse as a workshop,</i>

15:16.800 --> 15:20.740
<i>and I could afford the rent with the 
money from our potion contract.</i>

15:21.300 --> 15:24.150
<i>Master, where we now?</i>

15:24.150 --> 15:26.810
It's our new home.

15:26.810 --> 15:28.020
<i>Home?!</i>

15:28.490 --> 15:29.610
Well?

15:30.410 --> 15:31.980
I'll take it.

15:33.660 --> 15:36.690
We'll make arrangements so 
you can move in tomorrow.

15:37.040 --> 15:39.200
Yes, thank you.

15:44.060 --> 15:46.120
Are you curious about it?

15:46.550 --> 15:50.920
Yes. It's been bothering me 
since we arrived in this city.

15:50.920 --> 15:52.640
It's the smell of the sewage.

15:53.000 --> 15:54.130
Sewage?!

15:54.530 --> 15:56.300
The nobles use magical purifying devices

15:56.300 --> 15:59.590
to treat the sewage from
 their mansions, but...

15:59.970 --> 16:03.290
They don't use such magical 
devices in the city's sewers?

16:04.030 --> 16:08.760
Magic purifying devices have to be 
excavated from dungeons or ancient ruins,

16:08.760 --> 16:10.360
so they're too expensive.

16:11.020 --> 16:13.950
Then they don't purify the sewers at all?

16:13.950 --> 16:17.750
Some priests are hired to 
purify them periodically.

16:21.220 --> 16:24.800
<i>The next day, Maple and 
I moved into our new home.</i>

16:26.220 --> 16:29.600
<i>We'll handle repairing the 
outer walls at a later point,</i>

16:31.040 --> 16:32.720
<i>but first, we need that!</i>

16:33.970 --> 16:37.360
<i>Mix quartz into the clay I purchased 
from the Papek Company,</i>

16:37.360 --> 16:40.690
<i>use magic to shape it,
 and once it's dried out...</i>

16:41.480 --> 16:42.630
<i>add heat!</i>

16:45.190 --> 16:46.770
<i>Adjust the temperature.</i>

16:49.270 --> 16:52.810
<i>Shorten the time it needs to 
bake by using space-time magic.</i>

16:54.650 --> 16:57.240
<i>Stabilize its condition with alchemy.</i>

16:58.710 --> 17:00.650
<i>Dismiss the fire magic.</i>

17:00.650 --> 17:02.780
<i>Keep the time-shortening going for now.</i>

17:00.870 --> 17:05.330
<b>Job</b>

17:00.870 --> 17:05.330
<b>Alchemist</b>

17:00.870 --> 17:05.330
<b>has leveled up</b>

17:02.580 --> 17:05.330
<b>Skill</b>

17:02.580 --> 17:05.330
<b>Light Magic</b>

17:02.580 --> 17:05.330
<b>has leveled up</b>

17:03.080 --> 17:05.330
<b>Skill</b>

17:03.080 --> 17:05.330
<b>has leveled up</b>

17:03.080 --> 17:05.330
<b>Alchemy</b>

17:06.400 --> 17:07.770
<i>Shoot...</i>

17:07.770 --> 17:10.200
<i>That consumed a whole lot of mana.</i>

17:10.200 --> 17:12.300
<i>But it was worth it.</i>

17:13.050 --> 17:14.940
It's finished!

17:14.940 --> 17:16.910
Ah, this is a must-have!

17:16.910 --> 17:20.610
Even if I've been reincarnated, 
this familiar shape is the best!

17:22.530 --> 17:24.770
Papek, what's the matter?!

17:27.190 --> 17:29.400
M-Maple?! What did you do?!

17:30.150 --> 17:32.110
<i>Entertain him.</i>

17:32.360 --> 17:35.470
Only the children of the 
village would enjoy that!

17:35.470 --> 17:37.060
Ah...

17:37.640 --> 17:40.470
This comforting texture...

17:40.470 --> 17:45.290
is luring me into blissful slumber.

17:47.790 --> 17:50.950
I'm truly sorry about that.

17:50.950 --> 17:54.410
No, no, it was a little surprising, but...

17:54.750 --> 17:58.540
I'm sorry, could I borrow your restroom?

17:58.540 --> 18:00.670
Oh, it's that way.

18:01.960 --> 18:04.370
Listen, Maple. Be careful not to—

18:04.370 --> 18:05.760
Mr. Takumi!

18:06.140 --> 18:07.960
You used the restroom fast!

18:07.960 --> 18:10.140
Wh-What is that restroom?!

18:10.630 --> 18:12.460
This is called a toilet,

18:12.460 --> 18:14.660
and I attached a 
magical device to it.

18:16.180 --> 18:17.820
What kind of device?

18:18.210 --> 18:21.240
After finishing your business,
 it uses purification to break it down

18:19.110 --> 18:24.040
<b>Magical Device</b>

18:20.370 --> 18:24.040
<b>Decompose</b>

18:21.240 --> 18:24.040
into clean water and a small 
amount of inorganic material.

18:22.370 --> 18:24.040
<b>Drainage</b>

18:24.820 --> 18:26.490
Purification?

18:26.490 --> 18:30.950
Mr. Takumi, do you have an 
aptitude for light magic?

18:31.900 --> 18:36.120
It might be better not to show
 that magic to just anyone.

18:36.940 --> 18:39.950
Um, if you could please 
keep that confidential...

18:40.390 --> 18:42.310
I understand.

18:42.310 --> 18:44.090
By the way, Mr. Takumi.

18:45.810 --> 18:50.270
Could you make another fifty—no, 
another hundred of these?!

18:50.270 --> 18:52.580
One hundred toilets?!

18:50.270 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:52.770 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:52.900 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.020 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.150 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.270 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.400 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.520 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.650 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.770 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:53.900 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:54.020 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:54.150 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:54.270 --> 18:54.980
<b>Toilet</b>

18:55.000 --> 18:56.330
Please!

18:56.330 --> 18:59.460
Well, it should be manageable as 
long as I can get the materials...

18:59.460 --> 19:01.440
Thank you so much!

19:01.440 --> 19:03.210
Though with this...

19:03.810 --> 19:06.880
You'll need extra hands, Mr. Takumi.

19:06.880 --> 19:10.060
Well, I was planning to 
hire people eventually.

19:10.060 --> 19:12.600
I would recommend getting 
a contract with a slave.

19:12.600 --> 19:13.660
A slave?!

19:13.980 --> 19:17.580
Considering your talents and aptitude,

19:17.580 --> 19:20.600
I believe a slave bound to secrecy by 
contract magic would be best suited

19:20.600 --> 19:24.780
to serve as your protection 
and manage the mansion.

19:25.280 --> 19:27.520
To secrecy?

19:27.840 --> 19:30.980
You have an aptitude for light magic.

19:30.980 --> 19:34.010
That means you're "chosen by God,"

19:34.010 --> 19:38.700
or so the Church of the Divine Light that 
heads the Holy Empire of Sidonia insists.

19:38.950 --> 19:43.240
The Church scoops up anyone 
with aptitude for light magic,

19:43.240 --> 19:47.420
and profits from exploiting 
 their healing magic.

19:47.420 --> 19:49.830
I can't imagine they'd 
ignore purification magic

19:49.830 --> 19:52.880
like what this toilet
 being used by commoners.

19:53.170 --> 19:56.600
Huh? Is it even okay to produce them, then?

19:56.600 --> 20:01.300
I have some thoughts on how to 
gain the backing to support that,

20:01.300 --> 20:06.020
but we'll have to ensure that they
 do not know you are the one behind it.

20:06.820 --> 20:08.050
I see.

20:08.050 --> 20:12.260
So you should definitely form 
a contract with a slave.

20:11.340 --> 20:13.330
P-Please hold on a moment!

20:13.330 --> 20:15.720
I'm against using slaves.

20:16.650 --> 20:19.250
Is there something wrong with that?

20:19.250 --> 20:23.360
Well, I can't say the term 
leaves a good impression.

20:23.360 --> 20:25.190
But Mr. Takumi—

20:25.760 --> 20:28.130
If it means forming a 
contract with a slave,

20:28.130 --> 20:30.140
then I'd rather do everything by myself.

20:30.140 --> 20:32.360
No way! That's impossible.

20:32.740 --> 20:33.710
Hm?

20:33.710 --> 20:35.200
My guild card?

20:39.480 --> 20:41.230
<i>Takumi Iruma.</i>

20:41.230 --> 20:44.500
<i>You need to complete a quest 
of the appropriate level</i>

20:44.500 --> 20:47.890
<i>within one month of registering 
with the Adventurer's Guild.</i>

20:48.180 --> 20:50.510
<i>We're sorry to trouble 
you while you're busy,</i>

20:50.510 --> 20:55.380
<i>but we ask that you make your way to the 
Adventurer's Guild before the deadline.</i>

20:56.120 --> 20:57.480
A quest?

20:57.890 --> 21:01.320
I definitely do need extra hands.

21:02.290 --> 21:04.710
Do you have some time free today?

21:05.080 --> 21:05.860
Huh?

21:07.240 --> 21:13.940
The Mulan Company is the most 
trustworthy slave trader in Bolton.

21:14.540 --> 21:16.830
Please wait here a moment.

21:21.030 --> 21:22.880
What now?

21:30.150 --> 21:34.170
Wow, what a pretty garden.

21:54.070 --> 21:55.300
Go home.

21:55.650 --> 21:56.350
Huh?
